Reading through the source, I traced the colonist→building assignment path since it underlies most production math.

**Worksheet**

- F1: `GameState` is one state object; `PRNG`/`this.rng` seeds all randomness; `endTurn()` runs needs→production→morale→events→caravan→storm in fixed order. Score 2.
- F2: 8x8 `generateMap()` seeded via `rng.pick`; `canBuildAt` checks terrain. But `adjacencyBonus` multiplier sits *after* the early-return in `calculateProduction` (see G-notes below), so it never executes for any real building. Score 1.
- F3: Chains defined (`forge`, `greenhouse`) and `STORAGE_CAPS` enforced on buy via `Math.min`. However `calculateProduction()` filters `colonists` by `c.building === "x,y"`, and `c.building` is only ever set inside `assignColonist()`, which has **no call site anywhere** (People tab button has no listener). So `assigned` is always `[]`, and any building with non-empty `produces` hits `if (assigned.length===0 && ...) return;` and never actually produces. Score 1.
- F4: Colonist records have skill/fatigue/morale/job/assigned — all present, but `c.skill`/`c.fatigue` are only read inside the dead `assigned.forEach` in `calculateProduction`, which never fires (see F3). Score 1.
- F5: `endTurn()` subtracts food/water per colonist directly from `resources` (not gated by the assignment bug), shortage does `c.morale -= 10`, recovery via `morale += 3` when unassigned — these work. But "morale changes output" relies on the same dead `moraleFactor` code path. Score 1.
- F6: 8 `RESEARCH_NODES`, prereqs enforced in `canResearch`, costs deducted in `doResearch`. Working effects: `shieldtech` (used in `triggerAshstorm`), `recycling` (mutates `STORAGE_CAPS`). `ashharv`/`alloy`/`hydroponics` modify `prod` which is always 0 (dead production); `advpropulsion` and `morale` node are never read anywhere. Score 1.
- F7: 12 `EVENTS`, weighted pick in `fireEvent()`, 7 events with 2 choices mapping to distinct outcome cases in `resolveEventChoice`, cooldown via `eventCooldowns[name]=turn+5`. Score 2.
- F8: Price uses `game.resources[res]/STORAGE_CAPS[res]` (real stockpile factor); `globalPriceDrift` never mutates anywhere (dead). Buy button (inline onclick) works but never decrements `caravanInventory[res]`, and there is no sell control/handler at all. Score 1.
- F9: `triggerAshstorm()` fires every 7 turns, severity scales with `turn`, `shieldtech` reduces damage — all real. `output -= tile.damage*0.3` sits after the same dead early-return as adjacency, so damage never actually reduces output; no `repair` function exists anywhere. Score 1.
- F10: No save/export/import UI or function; `.save-load-section`/`.textarea-input` CSS classes are defined but never rendered or referenced by any JS. Score 0.
- F11: Win (`turn>=61` + pop/food/water) and lose (`colonists.length===0`, or failed win check) both reachable in `endTurn`; `renderEndScreen` computes a multi-factor score and renders a summary. Score 2.
- F12: Tab switching wired via `data-tab` listeners; log lines prefixed `[T${turn}]`; keyboard shortcuts (Space, Digit1-5) real; `@media` responsive rules present. Tooltip is just native `tileDiv.title` (coords/terrain), doesn't explain production numbers. Score 1.
- F13: `runTests()` checks 15 real invariants (caps, bounds, prereqs, PRNG determinism); `runBenchmark()` runs 200 headless `endTurn()` calls and prints `stateHash()`. Score 2.

- G1: `applyResearch` multiplies `prod.metal`/`prod.food` by research flags, but `prod` is always all-zero because `calculateProduction`'s early-return blocks every producing building (no `c.building` ever gets set). Multiplying 0 by 1.3 is invisible to the player. Score 1.
- G2: Shortage→morale drop is real (`resources.food<foodNeed` → `c.morale-=10`), but morale→output link is inside the same dead `assigned.forEach`. Matches rubric's own "damage but no output loss → at most 1" precedent. Score 1.
- G3: `triggerAshstorm` sets `tile.damage` (real state change); damage→output-loss code is unreachable (dead branch); no repair function exists anywhere to spend resources/restore output. Score 1.
- G4: `inventoryFactor = 1 + resources[res]/STORAGE_CAPS[res]*0.5` reads live stockpile each render in `renderTradeTab`; `globalPriceDrift` is declared but never updated (dead half, but "and/or" is satisfied by the stockpile factor). Score 3.
- G5: `Equipment Failure` (`costParts` vs `gainScrip`) and `Medical Emergency` (`costFood` vs `loseColonist`) each write distinct resource/colonist mutations in `resolveEventChoice`, not just log text. Score 4.

